  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-36" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-37" contextRef="c-1">Q2</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-38" contextRef="c-1">2026-06-30</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-39" contextRef="c-1">2026-06-30</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-40" contextRef="c-1">2026-06-30</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfApplicableNotesTextBlock id="f-41" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The notes provided herein were derived from the notes disclosed in the Quarterly Report of Exelon Corporation (Exelon) on Form 10-Q for the period ending June 30, 2026. The notes presented herein were modified to include information relevant to Commonwealth Edison Company of Indiana, Inc. (the Company). All amounts presented within the footnotes are rounded to the dollar unless otherwise noted. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;1. Significant Accounting Policies &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Description of Business&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company was organized in the state of Indiana on March 22, 1926. The operations of the Company consist principally of the transmission of electricity, primarily to Commonwealth Edison Company (ComEd). The Company&#8217;s transmission line interconnects the transmission systems of ComEd and Indiana Michigan Power Company, a subsidiary of American Electric Power Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company, a regulated electric utility, is a wholly-owned subsidiary of ComEd, which is a principal indirect subsidiary of Exelon. The Company's accounting policies for regulated operations are in accordance with those prescribed by the regulatory authorities having jurisdiction, principally the Indiana Utility Regulatory Commission (IURC) and the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). The accompanying financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in its Uniform System of Accounts (USOA) and accounting releases, which differ from accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (GAAP). The principal differences from GAAP include the exclusions of current maturities of long-term debt from current liabilities, the exclusion of debt issuance costs from long-term debt, the classification of accrued taxes as assets and liabilities rather than a net amount, the exclusion of FIN 48 liabilities related to temporary income tax differences, the derecognition of operating leases from the balance sheet, the classification of cloud computing costs, and the classification of certain other assets and liabilities between current and noncurrent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;New Accounting Standards&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;New Accounting Standards Issued and Not Yet Adopted as of June 30, 2026: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The following new authoritative accounting guidance issued by the FASB has not yet been adopted and reflected by the Company in its financial statements as of June 30, 2026. Unless otherwise indicated, the Company is currently assessing the impacts such guidance may have (which could be material) in its Balance Sheets, Statement of Income, Statement of Cash Flow and disclosures, as well as the potential to early adopt where applicable. The Company has assessed other FASB issuances of new standards which are not listed below given the current expectation that such standards will not significantly impact the Company's financial reporting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Disaggregation of Income Statement Expenses (Issued November 2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; Provides additional disclosure requirements related to relevant expense captions of income statement expense line items. The revised guidance requires a new tabular disclosure of disaggregated income statement expenses including a break out of (1) purchases of inventory, (2) employee compensation, (3) depreciation, (4) intangible asset amortization, (5) depreciation, depletion, and amortization recognized as part of oil and gas producing activities included in each relevant expense line item on the income statement. The tabular disaggregation should include certain amounts already required to be disclosed under GAAP elsewhere. Any remaining amounts not separately disaggregated quantitatively should include a qualitative description. Additionally, on an annual basis, the standard requires disclosure of management&#8217;s definition of selling expenses and the amount of expense. The standard is effective January 1, 2027, with early adoption permitted. The Company is currently assessing the impacts of this standard.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Environmental Credits and Environmental Credit Obligations (Issued May 2026). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Establishes guidance for the recognition, measurement, presentation and disclosure of environmental credits and compliance obligations that may be settled by using environmental credits. The guidance is effective for annual and interim periods beginning January 1, 2028 with early adoption permitted. The guidance is adopted on a retrospective basis by recognizing a cumulative effect adjustment to retained earnings at the date of initial application.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2. Fair Value of Financial Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;As of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025, the Company&#8217;s carrying amounts of cash, accounts receivable, and short-term investments are representative of fair value because of the short-term nature of these instruments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;3.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:70.626%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:12.739%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:12.740%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:3pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3